# PROTOCOL-AMENDMENTS.tsv.example — template for the machine-readable tracker
# consumed by coord-protocol-metrics.sh (amendments_unimplemented_display / count).
#
# Copy this file to PROTOCOL-AMENDMENTS.tsv beside coord-protocol-metrics.sh
# (or point COORD_AMENDMENTS_FILE at wherever you keep it) and replace the
# example rows below with your own protocol's ratified amendment items.
#
# PROTOCOL-VERSION: 1.0.0
#
# Columns: id<TAB>status<TAB>title
# status: pending | implemented | deferred | n/a-prompt
#   pending      — ratified, not yet built; counted in the "open" bucket
#   implemented  — shipped; not counted
#   deferred     — ratified but intentionally parked; reported as a separate
#                  bucket, not "open" (permanent-park items should not float
#                  the open-count floor forever)
#   n/a-prompt   — a prompt-discipline item with no mechanical equivalent yet;
#                  same non-open treatment as deferred
#
# "ratified-but-unimplemented" open count = pending only (actionable work).
# Lines starting with # are ignored by the parser.

item1	pending	Example: queue-depth floor mechanized in coord-status + heartbeat
item2	implemented	Example: PROTOCOL-VERSION stamp added to this protocol's README
item3	n/a-prompt	Example: evidence-paste discipline (prompt-only until mechanized)
SSH-MSG-AUTH-20260809	implemented	Message Authenticity (SSH signing) — coord-keygen.sh/coord-verify.sh, coord-send.sh always signs, precommit hard-block, bootstrap key handshake (PROTOCOL 1.4.0)
